{
  "name": "Autonomous Task Executor",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "description": "Enables autonomous overnight development with smart commit strategy",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "🌙 AUTONOMOUS DEVELOPMENT MODE\n\nSESSION CONTINUITY (FIRST STEP):\n1. Check for context transfer summary from previous session\n2. If present, READ IT to understand:\n   - What tasks were in progress\n   - What was just completed\n   - What should be done next\n   - Any blockers or issues\n3. Then read steering files and specs\n4. Make decision on what to work on next\n\nEXECUTE TASKS:\n\nFOR EACH TASK:\n1. Check CI/CD status: node scripts/check-cicd-status.js\n2. Wait if deployment in progress\n3. Implement fully (code + tests + docs)\n4. Commit: node scripts/safe-commit-push.js \"feat: [description]\"\n5. Monitor CI/CD deployment\n6. Continue to next task after deployment succeeds\n7. Do not stop after the task summary or status of what's been completed. Continue with the next task or feature\n\nFAILURE HANDLING:\n- Validation fails: Auto-fix and retry (max 3 attempts)\n- CI/CD fails: Analyze, fix, retry (max 2 attempts)\n- Still failing: Document and continue to next task or feature\n\nSESSION ENDING:\n- When notified the session is ending or being summarized, STOP immediately\n- Complete current commit if in progress, then stop\n- Do NOT start new tasks\n- The context transfer summary will allow the next session to continue seamlessly\n\nSee .kiro/steering/00-global.md for detailed rules."
  },
  "enabled": true,
  "workspaceFolderName": "budgetbuddy",
  "shortName": "autonomous-task-executor"
}